Z||000000||jmw||12-06-2000||08:22 PM||||This isn't really 'technical' but I posted  under General Chat and didn't get too much help. <P>First question: NTB has discontinued Pirelli Formula GTs (S-rated blackwalls) for $26 each + tax in my size (215/60/14). Supposedly they're comparable to BF Goodrich Radial T/A's ($50 + shipping, but no tax, at tirerack.com) which is what I was after to begin with. [BTW, NTB will match tirerack's prices]. My question is, are these Pirelli's truly comparable or should I stick with the BFGs? <P>Also, they charge $10 ea. to mount & balance,  $2.50 for stems, plus $54.99 for an alignment. Is this a fair price?  If not, what is?<P>Second question: NTB has Monroe shocks for $22.99 ea. + $11 ea. to install. Is that a fair price? If not, what is? <P>Third question: they have struts for $59.99 ea. + $34.99 ea. to install. Is that a fair price? If not, what is?<P>I am determined not to get gypped ever again so any advice y'all can offer would be greatly appreciated. [I have been doing some price checking online, but don't know one tire/shock/strut from another.]<P>Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||12-06-2000||09:24 PM||||Tire           $26.00<BR>Stem           $ 2.50<BR>Mounting/bal   $10.00<BR>______________________<BR>               $38.50<BR>Tax(?) 8%      $ 3.08<BR>_____________________<BR>                $41.58 x 4= $166.32<P>not a bad price for 4 tires.  The Goodriches will still need to be mounted and balanced + stems, so you can add $12.50+ tax to each Goodrich tire plus shipping.  I've paid more for my GT tires, but they are bigger.<P>Four wheel alignment for $55 + tax isn't bad, or is it a two wheel alignment?  Fieros need four wheel alignment.<P>All new suspension for $280 + tax, not bad, but I bet they suck you in for ball joints/tie rods.<P>You need to do some more comparison shopping in your area for the suspension work.  Check out the prices at an alignment specialty shop.<BR>||||reg||1
